{"step_index":1453,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-23T08:15:15Z","thinking":"The Colab URL suggests the training environment. Task-1450's error indicates a problem attaching to the target, likely due to a missing or misformatted session ID during the attachment attempt. Examining the `Target.attachToTarget` call is necessary to understand how the session ID is handled and where the error originates.\n\n\nAnalyzing the code, the session ID is extracted from the `attachToTarget` response; however, it appears that this response can be `None`. Investigating the `colab-mcp` tools, the initial Colab page appears to be a blank new notebook, not the target notebook. The active tab's CDP target ID is available. The `attachToTarget` call is suspect; the CDP connection to the target needs direct inspection.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"import asyncio\nimport json\nimport websockets\nimport sys\n\nsys.stdout.reconfigure(encoding='utf-8')\n\nBROWSER_WS = \"ws://127.0.0.1:9222/devtools/browser/25a8f755-6780-4694-b7aa-32d603640dd1\"\nTARGET_URL = \"https://colab.research.google.com/drive/1u6mCyiyeT45QW6O0L-95tJ-csN6VEC17#scrollTo=wj3SCRn_aJF3\"\n\nasync def main():\n    async with websockets.connect(BROWSER_WS) as ws:\n        # Create target directly or navigate existing\n        await ws.send(json.dumps({\"id\": 1, \"method\": \"Target.getTargets\"}))\n        res = json.loads(await ws.recv())\n        targets = res[\"result\"][\"targetInfos\"]\n        \n        colab_id = None\n        for t in targets:\n            if \"colab.research.google.com\" in t.get(\"url\", \"\") and t.get(\"type\") == \"page\":\n                colab_id = t[\"targetId\"]\n                print(f\"Found existing Colab target: {colab_id}\")\n                break\n                \n        # Send attach\n        await ws.send(json.dumps({\n            \"id\": 2,\n            \"method\": \"Target.attachToTarget\",\n            \"params\": {\"targetId\": colab_id, \"flatten\": True}\n        }))\n        attach_res = json.loads(await ws.recv())\n        print(\"Attach response:\", attach_res)\n        session_id = attach_res[\"result\"][\"sessionId\"]\n        \n        # Navigate using sessionId\n        await ws.send(json.dumps({\n            \"id\": 3,\n            \"sessionId\": session_id,\n            \"method\": \"Page.navigate\",\n            \"params\": {\"url\": TARGET_URL}\n        }))\n        nav_res = json.loads(await ws.recv())\n        print(\"Nav response:\", nav_res)\n        \n        # Also activate target to bring to front\n        await ws.send(json.dumps({\n            \"id\": 4,\n            \"method\": \"Target.activateTarget\",\n            \"params\": {\"targetId\": colab_id}\n        }))\n        print(\"Activated target.\")\n        \n        print(\"Waiting 10 seconds for Colab notebook to load...\")\n        await asyncio.sleep(10)\n        \n        # Check current URL\n        await ws.send(json.dumps({\n            \"id\": 5,\n            \"sessionId\": session_id,\n            \"method\": \"Runtime.evaluate\",\n            \"params\": {\"expression\": \"window.location.href\"}\n        }))\n        url_res = json.loads(await ws.recv())\n        print(\"Current page URL:\", url_res.get(\"result\", {}).get(\"result\", {}).get(\"value\"))\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    asyncio.run(main())\n","Description":"Navigate Colab target with valid session ID","Overwrite":true,"TargetFile":"c:\\Users\\k4ran\\OneDrive\\Desktop\\smartAGENT\\scripts\\nav_correct.py","toolAction":"Writing nav_correct.py","toolSummary":"CDP navigation script"}}]}
