{"step_index":1475,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-23T08:17:02Z","thinking":"The `nvidia-smi` command not found indicates the current session is using a CPU runtime, not the intended GPU. The target notebook, located at the provided URL, is specifically configured for a T4 GPU runtime. The primary challenge is to navigate the browser to this correct notebook.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"import urllib.request\nimport json\nimport sys\n\nsys.stdout.reconfigure(encoding='utf-8')\n\n# Read DevToolsActivePort\nwith open(r\"C:\\Users\\k4ran\\AppData\\Local\\Google\\Chrome\\User Data\\DevToolsActivePort\", \"r\") as f:\n    lines = f.read().splitlines()\n    port = lines[0]\n    path = lines[1]\n\nprint(f\"Port: {port}, Path: {path}\")\n\n# In modern Chrome, if you connect via WebSocket to ws://127.0.0.1:{port}{path}\nimport asyncio\nimport websockets\n\nasync def test():\n    uri = f\"ws://127.0.0.1:{port}{path}\"\n    print(f\"Connecting to {uri} with origin=None...\")\n    try:\n        # Note: headers={'Origin': 'http://127.0.0.1:9222'} or origin=None\n        async with websockets.connect(uri, origin=None, open_timeout=5) as ws:\n            await ws.send(json.dumps({\"id\": 1, \"method\": \"Target.getTargets\"}))\n            res = await ws.recv()\n            print(\"Response:\", res[:200])\n    except Exception as e:\n        print(\"Error:\", type(e), e)\n\nasyncio.run(test())\n","Description":"Test WebSocket connection to DevToolsActivePort","Overwrite":true,"TargetFile":"c:\\Users\\k4ran\\OneDrive\\Desktop\\smartAGENT\\scripts\\test_cdp.py","toolAction":"Testing CDP connection","toolSummary":"Test direct WebSocket to Chrome"}}]}
